## S1 REQ-I3: distinct daemon source, never operator

RED (sabotage): a bypassed validator that persists whatever source is
presented (mechanical equivalent of allowing the operator label for daemon
origin). Daemon-origin handoff labeled `From: operator` through the
bypassed validator:

```
SABOTAGED -> {'source': 'operator', 'action': 'persisted', ...}
```

The #81/#9 collision is restored: the daemon handoff is recorded as an
operator relay.

GREEN (restored): same handoff through the patched
`validate_handoff_source`, plus a genuine operator relay proving wave-9
handling is untouched:

```
PATCHED -> {'source': 'daemon:stuck-sweep', 'action': 'relabeled', ...}
PATCHED operator relay -> {'source': 'operator', 'action': 'persisted', ...}
```

Executable form: the S1d sabotage test in tests.test_seat_idle
(TestDaemonSource: bypassed -> operator collision; restored ->
daemon:stuck-sweep) and the genuine-operator-relay test (wave-9
attested/rejected preserved).
